      "description": "Watch Twente vs Qarabag highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The clash between Twente and Qarabag in the UEFA Conference League on August 20, 2026, delivered a masterclass in tactical discipline and European grit. Both sides entered the pitch with clear intentions, creating an atmosphere of high stakes from the very first whistle. A Physical Battle in the Opening Half The first half was characterized by a series of heavy challenges as both teams struggled to find a creative rhythm. The referee was kept busy throughout the period, issuing a flurry of cautions to maintain control. Robin Propper received the first yellow card in the 23rd minute, setting a tone of uncompromising defense. This was followed by a double booking in the 28th minute for Aske Adelgaard and Qarabag's Matheus Silva . As the interval approached, Daouda Weidmann also saw yellow, highlighting a gritty first 45 minutes where clear-cut chances were scarce. Malinowski Breaks the Deadlock The tactical stalemate was finally broken early in the second half. In the 52nd minute, Musa Gurbanly turned provider, delivering a precise pass to Kady Malinowski , who clinical finish sent the ball into the back of the net. The goal forced Twente to become more adventurous, leading to tactical substitutions as Sam Lammers and Kristian Hlynsson were introduced to spark an equalizer. Despite the increased pressure, Twente’s evening was further complicated by yellow cards for Ramiz Zerrouki and Daan Rots as they struggled to contain the visitors' counter-attacks. Closing Stages and Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, Twente threw everything forward, introducing Lucas Vennegoor of Hesselink and Filip Thorvaldsen in a late bid to salvage a point. Qarabag , however, remained resolute, managing the game professionally through their own substitutions and defensive organization. After five minutes of stoppage time, the referee blew the final whistle, confirming a vital victory for the visitors in a match where Malinowski’s strike proved to be the golden moment."
